id: 27
hanzi: 好奇
pinyin: hào qí
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Adjective

meanings_summary:
  en: curious; inquisitive; inquisitive interest
  es: curioso; inquisitivo; afán de saber

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Adjective | Standard | eager to know or learn something new, unusual, or unexplained | inclinado a conocer o averiguar cosas nuevas, raras o misteriosas | 对大自然抱有强烈的好奇心 (possess intense curiosity about nature)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 那个年幼的孩子趴在草地旁，好奇地观察着成群结队的黑蚂蚁如何分工搬运沉重的面包屑。 | Nà ge niányòu de háizi pā zài cǎodì páng, hàoqí de guānchá zhe chéngqún-jiéduì de hēi mǎyǐ rúhé fēngōng bānyùn chénzhòng de miànbāoxiè. | Lying upon the grass, the young child curiously observed how marching black ants divided labor to transport heavy breadcrumbs. | Tumbado en la hierba, el niño observaba con viva curiosidad cómo las laboriosas hormigas se repartían el acarreo de las migajas de pan.
  #2 | 保持对未知世界永不衰退的好奇与敬畏，是每一个真正科学家在漫长探索征途上最宝贵的动力源泉。 | Bǎochí duì wèizhī shìjiè yǒng bù shuāituì de hàoqí yǔ jìngwèi, shì měi yí ge zhēnzhèng kēxuéjiā zài màncháng tànsuǒ zhēngtú shang zuì bǎoguì de dònglì yuánquán. | Maintaining unfading curiosity and reverence toward the unknown is the most precious wellspring of motivation for any true scientist on the quest of discovery. | Preservar una curiosidad infatigable y reverencia ante lo ignoto constituye el motor más valioso de cualquier científico en su afán de saber.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  好奇心 | curiosity; inquisitive mind
  充满好奇 | filled with curiosity
  感到好奇 | feel curious about
  强烈的好奇 | intense curiosity
  满足好奇心 | satisfy one's curiosity
  好奇地打量 | scrutinize curiously

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  求知若渴 | qiú zhī ruò kě | thirsting for knowledge; eager intellectual yearning
  探幽索微 | tàn yōu suǒ wēi | probe deep mysteries and investigate subtleties
  别开生面 | bié kāi shēng miàn | break new ground; open up refreshing perspectives
  追本溯源 | zhuī běn sù yuán | trace back to the fountainhead; seek underlying origins

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  好 | hào | fond of; like; love; eager for | aficionado a; amar; gustar | 女 | woman | 女 (mother) + 子 (child embracing) | 好 (hào/hǎo) | 6 | 左右结构 | Mother 女 holding her child 子 with deep affection; fourth-tone reading (hào) denotes being fond of or inclined toward. | A loving mother (女) embracing her beloved child (子), fond of nurturing all that is good (好). | Una madre abnegada (女) abrazando a su tierno hijo (子), inclinada a amar y aprender (好). | 51 | VND | 好
  奇 | qí | strange; rare; wonderful; novel | raro; asombroso; singular | 大 | big | 大 (big / remarkable) + 可 (exclamation of approval) | 奇 (qí) | 8 | 上下结构 | Remarkable person 大 above approved speech 可; something extraordinarily striking, rare, and novel. | A person standing tall (大) exclaiming in astonishment (可) at a wondrous spectacle (奇). | Un hombre con brazos abiertos (大) exclamando con asombro (可) ante un prodigio singular (奇). | 35 | KMNR | 奇

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Being intensely fond of (好) exploring the strange and wonderful (奇) makes you curious (好奇).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Ser aficionado a (好) descubrir lo insólito y asombroso (奇) define a una persona curiosa (好奇).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Considered the prime catalyst of philosophical inquiry and scientific invention across Chinese intellectual traditions.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Falling fourth tone followed by rising second tone: 'hào qí' (51-35). Note fourth tone 'hào' (not third tone 'hǎo'), soaring upward on 'qí'.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    奇 | qí | strange; wonderful | Big 大 on top over 可
    夺 | duó | seize; snatch | Big 大 over 寸
    寄 | jì | send; mail; lodge | Roof radical 宀 on top of 奇
    椅 | yǐ | chair | Tree radical 木 on left of 奇
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
